IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tas-nouns`
IMPORT `tas-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania), ss 19 to 23: statutory instruments, exercise of powers, appointments, absence, regulations, rights, oaths.
-- Answers of a rule of reading: JUST TRUE where the text applies to the case; JUST FALSE only where the text itself says no to the case in its own words
--   (a "means" definition, a condition introduced with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless", a list closed with "only", a flat negative, a "where" that fails, a period the text fixes and the case falls outside it);
-- NOTHING everywhere else (an open list, "includes", a term left undefined, silence, a pointer outside the sources, a grant or prohibition limited by its own wording where the case falls outside the limit, a scope limit with no "only").
-- A rule that returns a day, a name or a value has no second not-covered answer, so it returns NOTHING when its text does not apply.
-- s 21(1A) is shown only as a row of dots and is not encoded.

§ `s 19: construction of statutory instruments`

-- src:365 | 19. Construction of statutory instruments
-- src:367 | Where an Act confers power to make, grant, or issue any regulation or other instrument, all expressions used in any such instrument shall have the same respective meanings as in the Act conferring the power.
@ref s 19 (src:365-367)
GIVEN `the Act confers power to make, grant or issue the regulation or other instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expression is used in the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19: the expression has the same meaning in the instrument as in the Act conferring the power` `the Act confers power to make, grant or issue the regulation or other instrument` `the expression is used in the instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the Act confers power to make, grant or issue the regulation or other instrument`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the expression is used in the instrument`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 19: the expression has the same meaning in the instrument as in the Act conferring the power` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19: the expression has the same meaning in the instrument as in the Act conferring the power` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 19: the expression has the same meaning in the instrument as in the Act conferring the power` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 20: exercise of powers and performance of duties`

-- src:373 | (a) from time to time as occasion may require; and
@ref s 20(a) (src:373)
GIVEN `the Act confers a power or imposes a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(a): the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion may require` `the Act confers a power or imposes a duty` MEANS
    IF `the Act confers a power or imposes a duty` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"

-- src:375 | (b) if conferred or imposed on the holder of any office, position or appointment as such, by the holder for the time being of such office, position or appointment.
@ref s 20(b) (src:375)
GIVEN `the Act confers the power or imposes the duty on the holder of an office, position or appointment as such` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the holder for the time being of that office, position or appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(b): the person is the one by whom the power is to be exercised and the duty performed` `the Act confers the power or imposes the duty on the holder of an office, position or appointment as such` `the person is the holder for the time being of that office, position or appointment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the Act confers the power or imposes the duty on the holder of an office, position or appointment as such`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- "if conferred or imposed on the holder ... as such"
           IF NOT (`the person is the holder for the time being of that office, position or appointment`) THEN NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 20(a): the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion may require` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(a): the power may be exercised and the duty shall be performed from time to time as occasion may require` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20(b): the person is the one by whom the power is to be exercised and the duty performed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 20(b): the person is the one by whom the power is to be exercised and the duty performed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 20(b): the person is the one by whom the power is to be exercised and the duty performed` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 21: power to appoint includes power to remove and the like`

DECLARE `Power that a power of appointment includes` IS ONE OF
    `a power to suspend or remove a person appointed under the power`
    `a power to reinstate or reappoint a person so suspended or removed`
    `a power to appoint some other person, temporarily, in the place of the person so suspended or removed`
    `a power to appoint some other person, temporarily, to the office or position because a person previously appointed is unable to carry out the duties`
    `a power to appoint some other person, temporarily, to the office or position because it is vacant`
    `some other power`

-- src:379 | (1) Where an Act confers a power to make any appointment to an office or a position, the power includes a power –
-- src:381 | (a) to suspend or remove a person appointed under that power;
-- src:383 | (b) to reinstate or reappoint any person so suspended or removed;
-- src:385 | (c) to appoint some other person, temporarily, in the place of the person so suspended or removed; or
-- src:387 | (d) to appoint some other person, temporarily, to the office or position –
-- src:389 | (i) where a person previously appointed is, for any reason, unable to carry out the duties of the office or position; or
-- src:391 | (ii) where the office or position is vacant.
@ref s 21(1) (src:379-391)
GIVEN `an Act confers a power to make an appointment to an office or a position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person appointed has been suspended or removed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person previously appointed is, for any reason, unable to carry out the duties of the office or position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office or position is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `Power that a power of appointment includes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1): the power to appoint includes the power` `an Act confers a power to make an appointment to an office or a position` `a person appointed has been suspended or removed` `a person previously appointed is, for any reason, unable to carry out the duties of the office or position` `the office or position is vacant` power MEANS
    IF NOT (`an Act confers a power to make an appointment to an office or a position`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
    ELSE CONSIDER power
        WHEN `a power to suspend or remove a person appointed under the power` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a power to reinstate or reappoint a person so suspended or removed` THEN IF `a person appointed has been suspended or removed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `a power to appoint some other person, temporarily, in the place of the person so suspended or removed` THEN IF `a person appointed has been suspended or removed` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `a power to appoint some other person, temporarily, to the office or position because a person previously appointed is unable to carry out the duties` THEN IF `a person previously appointed is, for any reason, unable to carry out the duties of the office or position` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- the "where" in paragraph (d)(i)
        WHEN `a power to appoint some other person, temporarily, to the office or position because it is vacant` THEN IF `the office or position is vacant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- the "where" in paragraph (d)(ii)
        WHEN `some other power` THEN NOTHING

-- src:395 | (1B) Where the power to appoint a person to an office or position is exercisable only on the recommendation, or with the approval or consent, of some other person, the powers conferred by subsection (1) are exercisable only on such a recommendation or, as the case may be, with such an approval or consent.
@ref s 21(1B) (src:395)
GIVEN `the power to appoint is exercisable only on the recommendation, or with the approval or consent, of some other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that recommendation, approval or consent has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1B): the powers conferred by subsection (1) are not exercisable` `the power to appoint is exercisable only on the recommendation, or with the approval or consent, of some other person` `that recommendation, approval or consent has been given` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the power to appoint is exercisable only on the recommendation, or with the approval or consent, of some other person`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `that recommendation, approval or consent has been given` THEN JUST FALSE   -- the "only" is satisfied
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- "exercisable only on such a recommendation"; none given

-- src:397 | (2) Any person appointed under a power referred to in subsection (1), by writing under his hand, addressed to the person who appointed him, may resign the office or position to which he was so appointed, and on acceptance of such resignation by the appointing person the office or position shall be vacated.
@ref s 21(2) (src:397)
GIVEN `the person was appointed under a power referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person resigns by writing under his hand, addressed to the person who appointed him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointing person accepts the resignation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(2): the office or position is vacated` `the person was appointed under a power referred to in subsection (1)` `the person resigns by writing under his hand, addressed to the person who appointed him` `the appointing person accepts the resignation` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the person was appointed under a power referred to in subsection (1)`) THEN NOTHING   -- a scope limit with no "only"
           IF NOT (`the person resigns by writing under his hand, addressed to the person who appointed him`) THEN NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording
           IF NOT (`the appointing person accepts the resignation`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- "on acceptance"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:401 | (a) he may be reappointed to that office or place at the expiration of that term if he is still qualified as prescribed by that Act; or
@ref s 21(3)(a) (src:401)
GIVEN `under a power conferred by an Act, a person is appointed to an office or place for a fixed term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided in that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is still qualified as prescribed by that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3)(a): the person may be reappointed at the expiration of the term` `under a power conferred by an Act, a person is appointed to an office or place for a fixed term` `the contrary is expressly provided in that Act` `the person is still qualified as prescribed by that Act` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`under a power conferred by an Act, a person is appointed to an office or place for a fixed term`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided in that Act` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the person is still qualified as prescribed by that Act` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- the text says "if he is still qualified"

-- src:403 | (b) if he is not so reappointed and no other person is appointed in his stead, the first-mentioned person may, until –
-- src:405 | (i) the date on which some other person is appointed in his stead; or
-- src:407 | (ii) a date not later than 6 months after the expiration of that term –
-- src:409 | whichever is the earlier date, continue to exercise and perform all the powers, authorities, functions, and duties conferred or imposed upon, or appertaining to, the holder of that office or place as validly and effectually for all purposes as if he had been duly reappointed thereto.
@ref s 21(3)(b) (src:403-409)
GIVEN `under a power conferred by an Act, a person is appointed to an office or place for a fixed term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressly provided in that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reappointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the term expired` IS A DATE
      `the day some other person is appointed in his stead` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(3)(b): the person may continue to exercise and perform the powers, authorities, functions and duties of the office on the day` `under a power conferred by an Act, a person is appointed to an office or place for a fixed term` `the contrary is expressly provided in that Act` `the person is reappointed` `the day the term expired` `the day some other person is appointed in his stead` `the day in question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`under a power conferred by an Act, a person is appointed to an office or place for a fixed term`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF `the contrary is expressly provided in that Act` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the person is reappointed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- the text says "if he is not so reappointed"
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `s 21(3)(b): the last day on which the holder may continue to exercise the powers after a fixed term` `the day the term expired` `with` `the day some other person is appointed in his stead`
               WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
               WHEN JUST lastDay THEN IF `the day in question` AT LEAST `the day the term expired` AND `the day in question` AT MOST lastDay THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- "until": outside the period

