§ `s 21A: performance of duties and the like in absence`

DECLARE `Kind of office for section 21A(1)(a)` IS ONE OF
    `an office, position or appointment arising from the appointment or employment of a person under the State Service Act 2000`
    `the office or position of a member, officer or employee of a State authority within the meaning of the State Service Act 2000`
    `a statutory office or any other office or position in the service of the Crown`
    `any other office, position or appointment`

-- src:413 | (1) Where –
-- src:415 | (a) by any enactment, instrument, contract or agreement, any duty, obligation, right or power is imposed or conferred on the holder of an office, position or appointment –
-- src:417 | (i) arising from the appointment or employment of a person under the State Service Act 2000; or
-- src:419 | (ii) being the office or position of a member, officer or employee of a State authority within the meaning of that Act; or
-- src:421 | (iii) being a statutory office or any other office or position in the service of the Crown; and
-- src:423 | (b) for any reason –
-- src:425 | (i) the holder of that office, position or appointment is unable to perform or exercise the duty, obligation, right or power; or
-- src:427 | (ii) that office, position or appointment is vacant –
-- src:429 | that duty, obligation, right or power may be performed or exercised by any eligible person so directed in writing by the appointing authority in the same manner and to the same extent in all respects as if that eligible person were the holder of that office, position or appointment.
@ref s 21A(1) (src:413-429)
GIVEN `a duty, obligation, right or power is imposed or conferred by an enactment, instrument, contract or agreement on the holder of the office, position or appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      office IS A `Kind of office for section 21A(1)(a)`
      `the holder is unable to perform or exercise the duty, obligation, right or power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office, position or appointment is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an eligible person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is directed in writing by the appointing authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21A(1): the person may perform or exercise the duty, obligation, right or power in the same manner and to the same extent as if the person were the holder` `a duty, obligation, right or power is imposed or conferred by an enactment, instrument, contract or agreement on the holder of the office, position or appointment` office `the holder is unable to perform or exercise the duty, obligation, right or power` `the office, position or appointment is vacant` `the person is an eligible person` `the person is directed in writing by the appointing authority` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a duty, obligation, right or power is imposed or conferred by an enactment, instrument, contract or agreement on the holder of the office, position or appointment`
                   AND (NOT (office EQUALS `any other office, position or appointment`))
                   AND (`the holder is unable to perform or exercise the duty, obligation, right or power` OR `the office, position or appointment is vacant`))
           THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF NOT (`the person is an eligible person` AND `the person is directed in writing by the appointing authority`) THEN NOTHING   -- a grant limited by its own wording
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:433 | appointing authority, in relation to an office, position or appointment, means –
-- src:435 | (a) in the case of an office, position or appointment to which appointments are required by or under an enactment to be made by the Governor – the Minister administering that enactment; and
-- src:437 | (b) in any other case – the person by whom appointments to that office, position or appointment are authorized to be made;
@ref s 21A(2) appointing authority (src:433-437)
GIVEN `appointments to the office, position or appointment are required by or under an enactment to be made by the Governor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister administering that enactment` IS A STRING
      `the person by whom appointments to that office, position or appointment are authorized to be made` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 21A(2): the appointing authority` `appointments to the office, position or appointment are required by or under an enactment to be made by the Governor` `the Minister administering that enactment` `the person by whom appointments to that office, position or appointment are authorized to be made` MEANS
    IF `appointments to the office, position or appointment are required by or under an enactment to be made by the Governor`
    THEN `the Minister administering that enactment`
    ELSE `the person by whom appointments to that office, position or appointment are authorized to be made`

-- src:439 | eligible person, in relation to an office, position or appointment, means a person who possesses the qualifications required by law to be possessed by the holder of that office, position or appointment;
@ref s 21A(2) eligible person (src:439)
GIVEN `the person possesses the qualifications required by law to be possessed by the holder of the office, position or appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21A(2): the person is an eligible person` `the person possesses the qualifications required by law to be possessed by the holder of the office, position or appointment` MEANS
    `the person possesses the qualifications required by law to be possessed by the holder of the office, position or appointment`

-- src:441 | enactment means –
-- src:443 | (a) an Act; or
-- src:445 | (b) any other instrument of a legislative character; or
-- src:447 | (c) any provision of an Act or of an instrument referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 21A(2) enactment (src:441-447)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `the instrument is of a legislative character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a provision of an Act or of such an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21A(2): the thing is an enactment` kind `the instrument is of a legislative character` `the thing is a provision of an Act or of such an instrument` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `an Act` OR `the instrument is of a legislative character` OR `the thing is a provision of an Act or of such an instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

