§ `s 22: power to make regulations and the like includes power to rescind and the like`

DECLARE `Power over an instrument` IS ONE OF
    `a power to rescind the instrument`
    `a power to revoke the instrument`
    `a power to amend the instrument`
    `a power to vary the instrument`
    `some other power over the instrument`

-- src:449 | 22. Power to make regulations, &c., includes power to rescind, &c.
-- src:451 | Where an Act confers a power to make any proclamations, rules, orders, regulations, or other instruments of a like nature, the power shall be construed as including a power exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions, if any, to rescind, revoke, amend, or vary any such instrument.
@ref s 22 (src:449-451)
GIVEN `an Act confers a power to make proclamations, rules, orders, regulations or other instruments of a like nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `Power over an instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22: the power includes the power` `an Act confers a power to make proclamations, rules, orders, regulations or other instruments of a like nature` power MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`an Act confers a power to make proclamations, rules, orders, regulations or other instruments of a like nature`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF power EQUALS `some other power over the instrument` THEN NOTHING   -- "including": an open list
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `the power to make the instrument is exercisable subject to a consent or condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22: the included power is exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` `the power to make the instrument is exercisable subject to a consent or condition` MEANS
    IF `the power to make the instrument is exercisable subject to a consent or condition` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- "if any"

§ `s 22A: power to grant a right includes power to vary or revoke`

DECLARE `Power over a right` IS ONE OF
    `a power to vary the right`
    `a power to revoke the right`
    `some other power over the right`

-- src:453 | 22A. Power to grant right includes power to vary or revoke
-- src:455 | A power in an Act to grant a right includes a power exercisable in a like manner and subject to the same consent and conditions, if any, to vary or revoke the right.
@ref s 22A (src:453-455)
GIVEN `an Act confers a power to grant a right` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `Power over a right`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22A: the power includes the power` `an Act confers a power to grant a right` power MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`an Act confers a power to grant a right`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- a failed "Where"
           IF power EQUALS `some other power over the right` THEN NOTHING   -- "includes": an open list
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `the power to grant the right is exercisable subject to a consent or condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22A: the included power is exercisable in a like manner and subject to the same consent and conditions` `the power to grant the right is exercisable subject to a consent or condition` MEANS
    IF `the power to grant the right is exercisable subject to a consent or condition` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- "if any"

#ASSERT `s 22: the power includes the power` TRUE `a power to rescind the instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22: the power includes the power` TRUE `a power to revoke the instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22: the power includes the power` TRUE `a power to amend the instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22: the power includes the power` TRUE `a power to vary the instrument` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22: the power includes the power` TRUE `some other power over the instrument` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22: the power includes the power` FALSE `a power to amend the instrument` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22: the included power is exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22: the included power is exercisable in the like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22A: the power includes the power` TRUE `a power to vary the right` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22A: the power includes the power` TRUE `a power to revoke the right` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22A: the power includes the power` TRUE `some other power over the right` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22A: the power includes the power` FALSE `a power to revoke the right` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22A: the included power is exercisable in a like manner and subject to the same consent and conditions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 22A: the included power is exercisable in a like manner and subject to the same consent and conditions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 23: power to determine includes power to administer an oath`

DECLARE `Authority of a person who hears and determines a matter` IS ONE OF
    `to receive evidence`
    `to examine witnesses`
    `to administer an oath to a witness lawfully called`
    `to take an affirmation from a witness lawfully called`
    `some other authority`

-- src:457 | 23. Power to determine includes power to administer an oath
-- src:459 | Any court, judge, justice, officer, commissioner, arbitrator, or other person authorized by law or by consent of parties to hear and determine any matter, shall have authority to receive evidence, and examine witnesses, and to administer an oath to, or take an affirmation from, all witnesses lawfully called before them respectively.
@ref s 23 (src:457-459)
GIVEN `the person is a court, judge, justice, officer, commissioner, arbitrator or other person authorized by law or by consent of parties to hear and determine the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      authority IS A `Authority of a person who hears and determines a matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23: the person has authority` `the person is a court, judge, justice, officer, commissioner, arbitrator or other person authorized by law or by consent of parties to hear and determine the matter` authority MEANS
    IF `the person is a court, judge, justice, officer, commissioner, arbitrator or other person authorized by law or by consent of parties to hear and determine the matter` AND NOT (authority EQUALS `some other authority`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 23: the person has authority` TRUE `to receive evidence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23: the person has authority` TRUE `to examine witnesses` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23: the person has authority` TRUE `to administer an oath to a witness lawfully called` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23: the person has authority` TRUE `to take an affirmation from a witness lawfully called` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23: the person has authority` TRUE `some other authority` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23: the person has authority` FALSE `to receive evidence` EQUALS NOTHING
